# Fault f_priced (writer 6): `value` of a place stated `priced v` crashed (KeyError). L §5.10 Value: "For a place of a
# `priced` kind, `value` uses its price"; L §5.7: "`priced p` values a place whose single position is valued by the price
# input p (tally 1's asset)"; the prelude's assets: "value = v at d". a is an asset stated `priced v` on its place
# section, v = 5.00 PLN (governs always): qa = 5 PLN. b is of the kind `valued: place PLN min 0 priced w`, w keyed by the
# kind, w[b] = 7.00 PLN: qb = 7 PLN (value doesn't round, L §5.10: a num PLN).
=== f_priced.tally
model fpriced
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "synthetic"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

kind valued: place PLN min 0 priced w

place a: assets PLN priced v lives 2026-01-01..

place b: valued lives 2026-01-01..

input v: money PLN

input w[x in valued]: money PLN

ask qa: value(a, 2026-06-30) in PLN law 2026-06-30

ask qb: value(b, 2026-06-30) in PLN law 2026-06-30

version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  v = 5.00 "row"
  w[b] = 7.00 "row"
=== expect
qa: 5 PLN
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-06-30
qb: 7 PLN
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-06-30
